<h2>Shingle or Metal for a Troy Home?</h2>
<p>Many Troy homeowners weigh asphalt shingles against metal when it is time for a new roof. Shingles usually cost less up front and suit most homes in town. Metal costs more to install but generally lasts longer, holds up well against wind and sheds summer heat effectively. It can also match the look of a metal barn or shop on the same property. Neither choice is right for everyone, and we are happy to compare both on your home during an inspection. Our <a href="/services/asphalt-shingle-roofing-temple-tx/">asphalt shingle roofing</a> page covers the shingle side of that decision.</p>

<h2>How We Handle Troy Inspections</h2>
